{
  "description": "Golden MessageIDs for fixed Any2TVMRampMessages. Cross-validates that the Go implementation (cciplib/ccip/codec/msghasher.go), the TypeScript implementation (contracts/src/offramp/generateMessageID.ts), and the Tolk implementation (contracts/contracts/ccip/offramp/types.tolk, exercised via contracts/contracts/test/lib/msg_hasher.tolk) all produce the same hash for the same message. Go tests only check their own implementation against these values; TypeScript tests check both the TypeScript and Tolk implementations against them. Golden values are anchored to the TypeScript/Tolk implementations (which match the on-chain OffRamp leaf recomputation); the Go hasher must agree with them. Conventions: big integers are decimal strings, byte strings are 0x-prefixed hex, TON addresses (receiver and token) are user-friendly base64, and tokenAmounts may be null (no tokens) or a list of token transfers whose extraData may be null (empty destPoolData from the source pool).",
